   200	### 3.1 Contract
   201	
   202	```
   203	expand-batch : datoms ctx → {:status :ok     :datoms out :root-eid r :log [...] :ctx ctx'}
   204	                          | {:status :error  :error {:kind ..} :log [...] :ctx ctx'}
   205	expand       : datoms ctx → out | throws                ; convenience over expand-batch
   206	definitions  : datoms → {sym lambda-ast|nil}           ; syntactic harvest, last wins; nil = removal
   207	drain-errors : expander → [expander' errors]           ; §5
   208	invoke       : lambda-ast operand-asts ctx → value      ; one body, §3.3
   209	valid-ast?   : value opts → nil | {:kind :invalid-output :at path}
   210	mark-tail    : ast → ast                               ; §3.4, whole-tree recompute
   211	step         : expander → expander'                    ; one forwarder step, §5
   212	event-schema                                           ; §4.1
   213	stdlib-forms, prelude
   214	```
   215	
   216	`ctx` is the expander's process state and is threaded through every call:
   217	
   218	```
   219	{:store    {sym lambda-ast}       ; macro environment, persisted across batches
   220	 :alloc    {:next-eid n}          ; monotonic negative counter, never re-seeded upward
   221	 :guards   {:max-depth 100  :max-nodes-per-expansion 10000
   222	            :max-steps 100000  :max-datoms-per-batch nil}
   223	 :eval     (fn [lambda-ast env prelude budget] → value)   ; §3.3
   224	 :t        0}                     ; batch counter; incremented once per expand-batch
   225	```
