   217	(defn run-on-stream
   218	  "Coordinate one `{:observer observer :consumer consumer}` session over the
   219	   attached medium, returning the updated session.
   220	
   221	   The consumer is any value the three supplied functions agree on. `ready?`
   222	   decides when it may accept another batch, `load` hands it one observed
   223	   batch and returns the successor consumer, and `run` lets it do whatever
   224	   work a loaded batch implies — evaluate, expand, index, forward — and
   225	   returns the successor. This is coordination, not interpretation: no field
   226	   of the consumer is inspected, so any consumer shape can be driven.
   227	
   228	   A consumer that is not ready runs first, and observation follows only if
   229	   it becomes ready. A ready consumer observes one batch; `gap` commits the
   230	   recovery cursor and continues; `blocked` and `end` return the session.
   231	   After a batch loads and runs, a consumer that is ready again observes the
   232	   next batch, and one that is not returns the session without another read.
   233	
   234	   A `load` or `run` that throws still propagates — the throw is kept — but
   235	   carries the partial session in the exception's data under `:session`, so
   236	   recovery is opt-in. Where the failure happened decides the carried
   237	   session: a throwing `load` carries the cursor *before* the failing batch,
   238	   so a retry re-reads it; a throwing `run` carries the cursor *after* the
   239	   loaded batch and the consumer the failing `run` left — the partial state
   240	   it reported under `:consumer` in its own exception's data when it made
   241	   progress before throwing, else the state `load` returned — so a retry
   242	   neither re-reads the batch nor repeats work already delivered; a
   243	   terminal read after processed batches carries the session those batches
   244	   produced. A consumer whose input can be bad should therefore return that
   245	   as data from `load` rather than throw, and reserve the throw for its own
   246	   defects."
